{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he took a wife, and her name was Keturah.</b> Even though an Israelite is forbidden [to marry] an Egyptian, as it is written: ״בנים אשר יולדו להם״ — the third generation may enter; the second generation may not. And Hagar was the daughter of Pharaoh, as Rashi explained above. One may say: he was a ger, and a ger is permitted [to marry] an Egyptian. And in the Midrash it is stated: he acted upon the instruction [from HaShem]."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The phrase 'על פי הדבור עשה' means Abraham acted on divine instruction; 'הדבור' rendered as 'the instruction' referring to divine speech."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:58.405110149Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}